{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's only message: \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\" CAMPAIGN.md (agent/CAMPAIGN.md) sets the goal: build a Synth SN50 price-simulation model with the lowest CRPS for CRYPTO_24H (BTC,ETH,SOL,XRP,HYPE; 24h, 5-min steps, 289 points), COM_EQU_24H (XAU,NVDAX,GOOGLX,TSLAX,AAPLX,WTIOIL,SPCX,SP500; SPYX is dead, ignore it) and CRYPTO_1H (crypto; 1h, 1-min steps, 61 points). The champion is evaluated over the 10 days after the 2026-09-14 data cutoff. Judge every experiment on CRPS, never on field-relative position. Work autonomously and record decisions in the journal. Keep working until a LANDING ORDER appears in agent/BUDGET.md; check BUDGET.md every iteration. Budget: 100 USD and 18h wall clock (at the last check: 2.53 USD used, about 0.4–0.6h elapsed; by now roughly 1.2h).\n\n   Constraints, preserved:\n   - No lookahead. Treat everything after 2026-09-14 as nonexistent. Querying ANY API (scores, rewards, dashboard) for times after 2026-09-14 invalidates the result, and the transcript is audited.\n   - Prices come from the snapshot only (market_data/, read-only). Never fetch market data online. The web is for knowledge only.\n   - Scoring goes through synth-lib (agent/predict.py / synth_lib.backtester). Never reimplement the metric.\n   - Do not falsify results. Do not copy another miner's served paths.\n   - Keep binary/encoded data out of the terminal: read parquet with pandas and never cat parquet, bundles or weights.\n   - Use public sources only. If any operator miner models turn up in the environment, leave them unread and note it in suggestions.md.\n   - Champion interface: agent/modeling.py `simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices)` returns `(start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths)`. Each path is a list of time_length//time_increment+1 floats starting at the last context price. Honour num_simulations. The model must tolerate NaN in context (drop, never interpolate) and must run OFFLINE.\n   - Any randomness must be seeded from the env var SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED, with a fallback seed when it is absent.\n   - Run every python command via `uv run`, from the workspace root.\n   - Deliverables in agent/: journal.md (per iteration: Hypothesis/Change/Result/Verdict/Lesson), report.md (context, approach, experiments including failures, results, limitations, what I'd do with more budget; audience: Synth miners), suggestions.md, and CHAMPION (YAML: sha = an existing commit, agent_dir: agent, profiles: [low, high], notes containing backtested CRPS per configuration from agent/predict.py at 1000 paths alongside the starter's CRPS). A champion is MANDATORY. Nominating is final: the first stop while agent/CHAMPION exists ends the campaign. Commit all deliverables. Target per-prompt latency is under about 5 s.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Validator scoring (synth/validator/crps_calculation.py):\n     - 24h: sum of CRPS in bps over 5min, 30min and 3h relative changes, plus the 24hour_abs price (CRPS/price×1e4).\n     - 1h: 1/2/5/15/30min changes, 60min_abs, and 12 \"gap\" intervals (change from t0 to 5k min).\n     - A vol-CRPS term applies from VOL_CRPS_1H_DATE = 2026-09-22 13:16:32 UTC (inside the eval window): 5.25 × mean CRPS of the std of 1-min returns per block (60/15/5 min). It is about 1% of the 1h CRPS.\n   - The backtester scores on field prompt start_times. Context ends at context_end(t) = t − lead(120s for 24h, 60s for 1h) − 60s. The realized path is the close of bars labelled t, t+step, …\n   - SYNTH_BACKTESTER_OFFLINE_DATA_ROOT is NOT set, so the backtester queries the live Synth API. Always use predict.py `--eval-end <= 2026-09-13`: the rewards query extends +24h, and 09-14 fails anyway because the 09-15 partition is missing.\n   - Field scores cached to cache/field/{ASSET}_{tl}.parquet, fetched from 2026-07-20 and capped at 2026-09-14T00:00Z.\n   - Realized validator paths live in market_data/realized/{asset}/{tl}_{ti}/ and are forward-filled. Exact-zero 5-min returns: equities/gold 4–16% (XAU 16%), BTC 0.4%.\n   - Volatility seasonality is modelled in America/New_York time (2016 five-minute-of-week bins).\n   - Horizon-bucketed log-HAR level forecast fitted by QLIKE. CRPS prefers a predictive variance below the mean variance.\n   - Innovations: Student-t per step times a per-path lognormal vol multiplier (optionally an OU process in log-vol).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - agent/predict.py (original, unchanged): the official backtest wrapper. Usage: `uv run agent/predict.py --asset BTC --days 3 --eval-end 2026-09-13 [--time-length 3600 --time-increment 60]`. Starter BTC-24h over 3 days to 09-13: mean_crps 2258.0 (69 prompts).\n   - agent/data.py: `load_asset(asset)` (lru_cached). Concatenates every market_data/prices/{asset}/1m parquet, returns a UTC timestamp index with OHLCV columns.\n   - agent/fetch_field.py: caches the field via get_miner_scores for 18 asset×tl jobs from argv start to CUTOFF=2026-09-14. Keeps columns miner_uid, asset, crps (float), scored_time, start_time, time_length. Skips files that already exist. All 18 are done.\n   - agent/fit_season.py: `--cutoff --days 180 --clip 50 --wd-pool 0.5 --smooth 0.2 --out`.\n     - Squared 1-min log returns (ffilled close) are divided by a centered 3-day rolling mean and clipped.\n     - Mean per NY bin; Mon–Fri get 50% pooling with the Mon–Thu average; 3-tap smoothing; normalised to mean 1.\n     - Outputs agent/artifacts/season_2026-08-01.npz and season_2026-08-29.npz. season.npz is currently a copy of the 08-01 profile; it must be refit to 09-14 for the champion.\n   - agent/harness.py:\n     - `evaluate(model_path, asset, tl, start, end, params, nsim, workers=14, stride, pool)` runs the model on field prompt times (hourly grid if there is no field file). The worker `_work` loads the model module and applies PARAMS.update(params).\n     - Context = df.loc[t−7d : context_end(t,tl)]. Real path via `_slice_real_prices` plus RealizedPathStore fill. Paths are cast to float32.\n     - Scoring calls calculate_crps_for_miner and calculate_vol_crps_for_miner, recording crps, crps_vol, i_* intervals, sec and cov, joined with field f_min/f_p10/f_med/f_n.\n     - `summarize()` reports vs_med%. The CLI takes --model --assets --tl --start --end --nsim --stride --params --out.\n   - agent/tune.py:\n     - WINDOWS: V1 = 2026-08-01→08-15 and V2 = 2026-08-29→09-13, each with its cutoff tag. Every variant gets season_file=agent/artifacts/season_{tag}.npz, har_file=har_{tag}.json and har_file_1h=har_{tag}.json. A \"{W}\" placeholder in a param string is replaced by the tag.\n     - GROUPS: C24, E24, C1H.\n     - It snapshots the model to results/snap_<ms>.py first. Paired variants run through a ThreadPool over a shared 14-process pool, and it prints the % change vs the first variant per asset, window and group.\n     - Usage: `uv run agent/tune.py '<variants json>' '<kwargs json e.g. {\"stride\":3,\"model\":...,\"groups\":[...]}>'`. Default stride is 2.\n   - agent/volstudy.py: `zseries` computes deseasonalized z; QLIKE of single EWMAs. Best half-life: 60–240 min for a 1h target, 720–1440 min for 24h.\n   - agent/harfit.py (split date arg): QLIKE fit of the log-HAR per group (crypto/equ). HLS=[15,60,240,720,1440]; BUCKETS=[(0,5),(5,15),(15,60),(60,180),(180,480),(480,1440)]; features log(EWMA/l7d) clipped to ±6 plus an intercept. Writes agent/artifacts/har_{split}.json {hls, buckets, coefs:{crypto/equ:{\"y{a}_{b}\": beta}}}. Out-of-sample it beats v1 everywhere. har.json is currently a copy of har_2026-08-29.json.\n   - agent/harcrps.py: Gaussian-CRPS-fitted HAR, producing harc5_*.json and harc1_*.json. Discarded.\n   - agent/research_oracle.py (research only, uses the future): wraps modeling, and when PARAMS[\"oracle_mode\"] is \"flat\" or \"buckets\" it replaces M._har_level with the realized future level. The default is \"off\".\n   - agent/modeling.py (current champion candidate, \"m2\"). Key structure:\n     ```python\n     PARAMS = {\"season_file\": HERE/\"artifacts\"/\"season.npz\", \"hl_short\":60., \"hl_med\":360., \"w_short\":0.3, \"w_med\":0.3,\n       \"tau_short\":240., \"scale\":1.0, \"nu\":5.0, \"sv\":0.25, \"sv_inf\":None, \"kappa\":0.0, \"seed\":12345,\n       \"har_file\": HERE/\"artifacts\"/\"har.json\", \"har_file_1h\": None,\n       \"groups\": {\"C24\":{\"scale\":0.75,\"sv\":0.4}, \"E24\":{\"scale\":0.9,\"sv\":0.4}, \"C1H\":{\"scale\":1.0,\"sv\":0.4}}}\n     ```\n     - `_season(asset)` returns ones when season_file is \"none\". `_minute_profile(prof, idx)` looks up NY bins. `_ewma_level(z, hl)` uses absolute-position weights and skips NaN.\n     - `_har(asset, time_increment)` picks har_file_1h when ti==60 and it is set, and returns (spec, coefs[crypto|equ]). `_har_level(z, har, h_min)` returns l7·exp(interp over log bucket midpoints).\n     - simulate:\n       1. grp = C1H if ti==60, else C24/E24; p = {**PARAMS, **groups[grp]}.\n       2. seed = int(os.environ.get(\"SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED\", p[\"seed\"])).\n       3. z = r²/profile over the context, using the ffilled log close.\n       4. Future minutes t0+1…t0+n_min with h = arange(1, n)+3. L = HAR level (or the v1 blend when har is \"none\").\n       5. v = scale·L·s_fut, summed into steps. eps = t(nu)·sqrt((nu−2)/nu). mult = the constant lognormal exp(sv·Z − sv²), or the OU path when kappa>0 or sv_inf≠sv.\n       6. inc = eps·sd·mult − 0.5(sd·mult)²; paths = last·exp(cumsum) with a leading zero column; returns `(start_time, time_increment, *paths.tolist())`.\n   - agent/baseline_starter.py: the starter model plus `PARAMS = {}`.\n   - agent/journal.md: entries 0–6 written (setup, v1, ablations, vol study, HAR+calibration, CRPS-HAR discarded, field standing).\n   - Commits: 909304b (v1), then \"HAR vol level, per-group calibration, CRPS-HAR study, oracle harness\". Git user was set locally: agent@campaign.local / \"campaign agent\". Commit messages end with \"Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\".\n   - results/ holds result files (m2_2026-08-01.parquet, m2_2026-08-29.parquet, tune*.txt) and snapshots (results/modeling.py, results/data.py, results/research_oracle.py are copies used by the oracle snapshot). cache/ and results/ are not in .gitignore, so avoid committing large files (commit only agent/).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - predict.py with eval-end 09-14 tried to write the missing 09-15 partition (read-only mount). Fix: use eval-end ≤ 09-13.\n   - The git commit failed with no identity. Fix: set user.email/name in the repo config.\n   - The field fetch crashed on a pyarrow object column (prompt_score). Fix: keep the needed columns only and cast crps to float; skip existing files.\n   - Editing modeling.py while tune ran broke the running workers (har.json missing). Fix: tune.py now snapshots the model file.\n   - `pkill -f tune.py` killed my own shell command (exit 144). Run pkill in a separate command.\n   - harcrps's L-BFGS did not converge (tiny gradients). Fix: normalise the loss by mean base sd and set tight gtol/ftol.\n   - \"none\" season_file raised FileNotFoundError. Fix: handled in _season.\n\n5. Problem Solving (results so far; % mean CRPS change, paired):\n   - v1 vs starter: every asset-config improves by 2–16%.\n   - Flat seasonality costs +7.5% on E24, +2% on C24, +1.5% on C1H.\n   - HAR+sv0.4 vs v1: C24 +0.07, E24 −0.95, C1H −0.61. Scale 0.8 then gives C24 −0.40.\n   - CRPS-HAR: no gain. OU vol: about the same as a scale change.\n   - m2 vs field median, V1: C1H −0.08…−0.38, C24 −0.10…+0.24, E24 −0.50…+0.46. V2: crypto about 0, E24 +0.6…+2.3 (AAPLX, SPCX, TSLAX, XAU worst). The field p10 is about 1–2% below the median.\n   - Latest breakdown of prompts by NY weekday: equities lose heavily on Friday (dow 4: +2.4…+7.2%) and Saturday (dow 5: +1.3…+7%), and are roughly flat or better on other days. By hour, Friday 12–24h NY is +9…+12.5% and Saturday 0–9h is +6…+9%. Crypto loses +1.4…+2.4% on Friday daytime. So 24h prompts that span Friday afternoon into the weekend are over-dispersed (or otherwise mis-specified). Likely causes: the level forecast carries weekday vol into the weekend; the weekend profile shape/levels are not right; or the realized paths are flat (zero returns) through the weekend market closure, so a point mass at zero or a much lower weekend variance is needed.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Read the oracle experiment result in results/tune_oracle.txt (variants base / oracle_flat / oracle_bk; stride 3; model agent/research_oracle.py).\n   - Fix the Friday/weekend weakness (weekend profile, zero-return mass, level handling across the weekend transition).\n   - Further ideas: point mass at zero for thin assets/closures; FOMC on Sep 16 2026, 14:00 ET, inside the eval window; range-based or cross-asset HAR features; tuning nu/sv per group; checking the 1h vol term.\n   - For the final champion: refit season.npz and har.json with cutoff 2026-09-14 (all data), run agent/predict.py at 1000 paths for each config and representative assets, compare with the starter, write report.md and suggestions.md (note the missing offline bundle / live API use), commit, and write agent/CHAMPION with sha, agent_dir: agent, profiles: [low, high] and notes with CRPS per configuration. Check BUDGET.md each iteration for a LANDING ORDER.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just run the per-prompt analysis of m2 vs field median by NY weekday and hour, using results/m2_2026-08-01.parquet and results/m2_2026-08-29.parquet. It showed the Friday/Saturday loss described above. The oracle tuning run was going in the background at that point, writing to results/tune_oracle.txt.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Read results/tune_oracle.txt for the oracle bound. Then investigate the Friday-to-weekend loss: compare realized vs predicted variance by NY day and hour for equities, check whether the validator realized paths are flat over weekends/closures, and test fixes such as a lower weekend profile, an adjusted HAR level across the weekend transition, or zero-return mass, using agent/tune.py paired runs on V1+V2. After that, update journal.md and commit.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-workspace/2d6fedfa-14d9-4a81-8f98-858ec201a373.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d6fedfa-14d9-4a81-8f98-858ec201a373","uuid":"d7b23c10-d195-4e73-a2f3-39ecc87a97e2","timestamp":"2026-09-30T05:59:37.683Z","isSynthetic":true}
