{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XokmZWk4LNa99pCRNWnr4n","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Synth subnet 50 miner model CRPS price paths approach GARCH tips\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Synth Subnet: AI-Driven Synthetic Data\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/961742741/Synth-Whitepaper-v1\"},{\"title\":\"Synth Price: SN50/USD Live Price Chart, Market Cap & News Today ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.coingecko.com/en/coins/synth-2\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - synthdataco/synth-subnet · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet\"},{\"title\":\"Your Simple Guide to Synth (SN50)\",\"url\":\"https://simplytao.ai/blog/your-simple-guide-to-subnet-50-synth\"},{\"title\":\"synth-subnet/README.md at main · synthdataco/synth-subnet\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet/blob/main/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction\",\"url\":\"https://docs.synthdata.co/\"},{\"title\":\"Mode launches Synth 'subnet' on Bittensor to build decentralized ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.theblock.co/post/337156/mode-launches-synth-subnet-on-bittensor-to-build-decentralized-ai-that-predicts-crypto-prices\"},{\"title\":\"synth-subnet\",\"url\":\"https://mode-network.github.io/synth-subnet/\"},{\"title\":\"Synth - Subnet Alpha\",\"url\":\"https://subnetalpha.ai/subnet/synth/\"}]\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - synthdataco/synth-lib · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-lib\"},{\"title\":\"Your Simple Guide to Synth (SN50)\",\"url\":\"https://simplytao.ai/blog/your-simple-guide-to-subnet-50-synth\"},{\"title\":\"Synth (SN50) LLM for Traders Launches on Polymarket & More\",\"url\":\"https://simplytao.ai/blog/synth-sn50-llm-for-traders\"},{\"title\":\"Synth Price: SN50/USD Live Price Chart, Market Cap & News Today ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.coingecko.com/en/coins/synth-2\"},{\"title\":\"Machine Allocators Don't Want Your Best Guess\",\"url\":\"https://www.abittensorjourney.com/p/synth-sn50-the-subnet-that-sells\"},{\"title\":\"Probability Clouds Over Price Predictions: How Synth SN50 Gets ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.synapz.org/posts/2025-06-19-synth-sn50-mandelbrot-validation\"},{\"title\":\"Synth\",\"url\":\"https://synthdata.co/\"},{\"title\":\"Bittensor Subnet 50:Synth - Bittensor123\",\"url\":\"https://bittensor123.com/subnets/sn50/\"},{\"title\":\"Estimating real-world probabilities: A forward-looking behavioral framework\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.09041\"}]\n\nI searched for Synth miner and GARCH information. The results explain clearly what miners are scored on. None of them gave GARCH tuning advice specific to Synth, so the GARCH tips at the end are my own general suggestions, not something the sources say.\n\n## What miners submit\n- The subnet asks miners for price paths that show their view of the future price distribution. Those paths should include realistic price dynamics, such as volatility clustering and skewed fat tailed price change distributions.\n- Miners submit ensembles of simulated price paths for a basket of crypto, equity, and commodity assets across two timeframes (24h and 1h). In November 2025, the network upgraded to 1,000 simulated paths, up from the original 100.\n- The listed assets are BTC, ETH, XAU, SOL, SPYX, NVDAX, TSLAX, AAPLX, and GOOGLX (note that CRPS for each asset contributes equally to final miner weights).\n- The two horizons use different step sizes. High-frequency forecasts cover 1-hour horizons with 1-minute increments and refresh every 12 minutes. Daily forecasts cover 24-hour horizons with 5-minute increments and refresh every hour.\n\n## How CRPS scoring works\n- CRPS is computed on the paths directly, without the need to construct an explicit probability distribution.\n- The system calculates CRPS on price changes measured in basis points across multiple time increments, including 5 minutes, 30 minutes, 3 hours, and 24 hours. The score rewards two things: calibration (do your predicted price changes align closely with observed market movements?) and sharpness (is your forecast distribution tight and precise, rather than overly broad?)\n- Scores are averaged over a rolling window and allocate emissions via softmax — equally split between 3 competitions: Crypto 1h, Crypto 24h, Commodities/Equities 24h. Lower CRPS → more emissions. The versions I found disagree on some details. The current README says the 1h window is 5 days and emissions are split three ways. Another indexed copy says 3 days for 1h with a 50/50 split. Check the live repo for the current rules.\n\n## Tools and approaches\n- **Backtesting:** synthdataco/synth-lib provides tools for downloading minute-level market data and backtesting miners against Synth Subnet scoring. A backtest computes CRPS per prompt, and then replays the validator's smoothed-score / reward-weight calculation to produce the miner's rank over time. The same repo points to a miner tutorial for newcomers.\n- **Baseline to beat:** CoinGecko says the combined network model consistently outperforms standard benchmarks like Geometric Brownian Motion. Plain GBM won't be competitive.\n- **Focus on volatility:** Founder James Ross puts it, modeling raw price is nearly impossible, but you *can* continuously improve at modeling volatility.\n- **Other models:** Synth's site describes a Chronos-2 miner fine-tuned with LoRA on a single consumer GPU, now competing live on the subnet.\n\n## GARCH tips (my suggestions, not from the sources)\n1. **Model returns in log or bps terms,** matching how CRPS is scored. Rescale before fitting, since the `arch` package prefers returns ×100.\n2. **Use fat-tailed, skewed innovations.** Try Student-t or skew-t instead of Gaussian. Also try GJR-GARCH or EGARCH to capture the leverage effect.\n3. **Fit separate models per horizon.** 1-minute data for the 1h contest and 5-minute data for the 24h contest behave differently. Add intraday seasonality, especially around US market hours for the equity tokens and XAU.\n4. **Keep the mean drift near zero.** Most of the gain comes from the volatility forecast, not the direction.\n5. **Watch calibration and sharpness together.** If the paths are too wide, you lose on sharpness. If they're too narrow, fat-tail moves will cost you. Try scaling the forecast volatility up or down in a backtest and pick the level that gives the lowest CRPS at all four scored intervals.\n6. **Refit often** on a rolling window, and try filtered historical simulation (bootstrapping standardized residuals) to get realistic tails.\n7. **Keep the path shape consistent.** Paths should be simulated step by step, so that the 5-minute, 30-minute, 3-hour and 24-hour changes all fit together.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d6fedfa-14d9-4a81-8f98-858ec201a373","uuid":"7e463aa6-1ce5-4b44-a5c6-e24c8daed29c","timestamp":"2026-09-30T06:57:45.442Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Synth subnet 50 miner model CRPS price paths approach GARCH tips","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Hc2bXBNLzWmsnigDesfbnp","content":[{"title":"Synth Subnet: AI-Driven Synthetic Data","url":"https://www.scribd.com/document/961742741/Synth-Whitepaper-v1"},{"title":"Synth Price: SN50/USD Live Price Chart, Market Cap & News Today ...","url":"https://www.coingecko.com/en/coins/synth-2"},{"title":"GitHub - synthdataco/synth-subnet · GitHub","url":"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet"},{"title":"Your Simple Guide to Synth (SN50)","url":"https://simplytao.ai/blog/your-simple-guide-to-subnet-50-synth"},{"title":"synth-subnet/README.md at main · synthdataco/synth-subnet","url":"https://github.com/synthdataco/synth-subnet/blob/main/README.md"},{"title":"Introduction","url":"https://docs.synthdata.co/"},{"title":"Mode launches Synth 'subnet' on Bittensor to build decentralized ...","url":"https://www.theblock.co/post/337156/mode-launches-synth-subnet-on-bitte