{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZCNkdSqQ4DKsfH5Ldxj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've nominated the champion (`agent/CHAMPION`, sha 1154d30) and committed everything. That ends the campaign, even though BUDGET.md never showed a LANDING ORDER: 2 of 18 hours and $7.90 of $100 were used. I stopped because the last five experiments all moved CRPS by under ±0.3%, and the direction flipped between my two test windows. More tuning at that point would mostly fit noise.\n\n**Where the model stands.** These numbers are out-of-sample: the model was fitted only on data before 08-29 and tested on 08-29 to 09-13 at 1000 paths.\n- **Against the starter:** better on every asset. By 2.8–19.5% on the 24h assets (equities gain the most) and by 4.9–9.1% on crypto 1h.\n- **Against the field:** within −0.67% to +0.72% of the per-prompt median. The best single miner that covered most prompts beats it by only 0.2–1.6%.\n\n**What made the difference this session:**\n- **Weekend variance fix.** The weekly profile divided returns by a 3-day rolling average, which overstated weekend volatility 2–3×. Equity prompts running from Friday into the weekend were losing 2–12% to the field median. Averaging over a whole week instead improves equities by about 0.6–0.9%.\n- **FOMC release.** The Fed statement is scheduled for 16 Sep 14:00 NY, inside the evaluation window. Crypto volatility runs 4–6× normal for the first 30 minutes after a release. Adding a multiplier around the release improved CRPS on four past FOMC days: −0.7% on overlapping 24h prompts and −1.2% on 1h prompts. The multipliers were estimated partly from those same days.\n- **Tried and dropped** (all within about ±0.3%):\n  - a point mass at zero for stale or closed markets\n  - resampling historical returns instead of Student-t steps\n  - varying the variance scale by horizon\n  - re-tuning scale, tail thickness and the per-path volatility spread\n- **Headroom check.** Even a model told the realised future volatility gained under 1% (research only; it uses future data), so better volatility forecasting has little left to give.\n\n**Scoring caveat.** `agent/predict.py` cannot score any equity or HYPE. synth-lib's price store refuses any window with a missing minute, and those assets have gaps every week. Those numbers in CHAMPION therefore come from my harness, which uses synth-lib's own CRPS functions on the field's prompt times. BTC, ETH, SOL and XRP were scored with `predict.py`. A rerun of the final commit reproduces BTC-24h exactly (2121.04). The windows quoted in CHAMPION overlap the data the final model was refitted on; the out-of-sample figures above are the fair comparison.\n\nEverything is in `agent/`: `report.md` (approach, results, lessons for miners), `journal.md` (17 entries), `suggestions.md` (including the missing offline backtest bundle and the missing-minute problem) and `CHAMPION`. No operator miner models turned up in the environment."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1479,"cache_read_input_tokens":145805,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1479,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2d6fedfa-14d9-4a81-8f98-858ec201a373","uuid":"a4f491c6-bf27-4504-ba9e-5662065b4e00","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:03:55.839Z"}
